  "name": "Dub Chamber",
  "tagline": "An echo hall: chords come back in new places, the colour shifts.",
  "description": "An echo hall. Dub chords are thrown into a long tape delay, so they come back in new places, and their colour shifts every few minutes. Glass tones answer from the room. A soft kick, a rolling sub, wide air.",
  "use": {
    "name": "Fuse",
    "for": "Contextual fusion: combining ideas across domains.",
    "why": "Your plan's Fuse state. Deep Work's steady pulse and quiet floor stay, so the contexts you are holding stay held. The associative side is loosened: chords that return in new places through the delay, a chord colour that shifts every few minutes, more air and space, and changes a little more often. Evidence that sound aids divergent thinking is weak; the Lab will decide."
  },
